==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|trials and errors}}

# The process of finding a solution to a problem by trying many possible solutions and learning from mistakes until success is attained.
#: {{ux|en|Navigating by '''trial and error''' may get you there eventually, but using a map is faster.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=A. A. Dowd|title=The Star and Director of ''{{w|La La Land}}'' Reunite for ''[[w:First Man (film)|First Man]]''’s Spectacular Trip to the Moon|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200616003944/https://film.avclub.com/the-star-and-director-of-la-la-land-reunite-for-first-m-1829631922|archivedate=16 June 2020|work=w:The A.V. Club|date=9 October 2018|passage='''Trial and error''' was a big part of the process: "We need to fail down here so we don't fail up there," [[w:Neil Armstrong|[Neil] Armstrong]] insists, though even some of the mistakes and malfunctions at ground level cause devastating casualties.}}

